# 🧠 1. Variable Declaration (var, let, const)

## 🔹 `var`

```js
var a = "TpointTech";
```

👉 Old way (ES5)
👉 **Function scope** hota hai
👉 Re-declare & re-assign dono allowed

⚠️ Problem:

* Block scope nahi hota → bugs create karta hai

---

## 🔹 `let`

```js
let a = 20;
```

👉 Modern JavaScript (ES6)
👉 **Block scope** ({} ke andar hi chalega)
👉 Re-assign allowed, re-declare ❌

---

## 🔹 `const`

```js
const p = "TpointTech";
```

👉 Value change nahi kar sakte ❌
👉 **Block scope**
👉 Always initialize karna padta hai

---

