# 🧠 JavaScript `let` Keyword (Complete Notes)

---

# 🔹 1. What is `let`?

```js
let variable_name;
```

👉 `let` ES6 (2015) me introduce hua
👉 Ye **block-scoped variable** create karta hai

---

# 🔹 2. Scope of `let`

## ✅ Global Scope

```js
let x = 20;

function show() {
  console.log(x);
}

console.log(x); // 20
show(); // 20
```

👉 Function ke bahar declare → global access ✔️

---

## ✅ Function Scope

```js
function show() {
  let num = 15;
  console.log(num); // ✅
}

console.log(num); // ❌ error
```

👉 Function ke andar → bahar access nahi ❌

---

## ✅ Block Scope (MOST IMPORTANT 🔥)

```js
{
  let num = 30;
  console.log(num); // ✅
}

console.log(num); // ❌ error
```

👉 `{}` ke andar hi accessible
👉 Ye `var` se biggest difference hai

---

# 🔁 3. Redeclaration Rules

```js
let a = 10;
let a = 20; // ❌ error
```

👉 Same scope me redeclare allowed nahi

---

## ✅ Different blocks me allowed

```js
{
  let a = 10;
}
{
  let a = 20;
}
```

👉 Alag blocks → alag memory

---

# 🔄 4. Re-assignment

```js
let a = 10;
a = 20; // ✅ allowed
```

👉 Value change kar sakte ho ✔️

---

# 🔥 5. let vs var (Core Difference)

## 🔹 Example (Block Scope)

### ❌ var

```js
function test() {
  if (true) {
    var x = 20;
  }
  console.log(x); // 20
}
```

---

### ✅ let

```js
function test() {
  if (true) {
    let x = 20;
  }
  console.log(x); // ❌ error
}
```

👉 Conclusion:

```text
var → function scope
let → block scope
```

---

# 🔁 6. Loop Scope (Very Important)

## ✅ let (Correct behavior)

```js
let i = 4;

for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
}

console.log(i); // 4
```

👉 Loop ka `i` alag hai
👉 Outer `i` safe hai

---

## ❌ var (Problem)

```js
