# 🔥 Step 1: Hoisting kya hota hai?

👉 JavaScript code run hone se pehle:

* Variables ko **memory me upar le jata hai (hoist karta hai)**

---

## 🔹 `var` case

```js
console.log(a);
var a = 10;
```

👉 JS internally aise treat karta hai:

```js
var a;           // hoisted
console.log(a);  // undefined
a = 10;
```

👉 Isliye `undefined` milta hai ✔️

---

# ❗ Ab `const` case

```js
console.log(x);
const x = 10;
```

👉 JS internally:

```js
// x hoisted hota hai (memory me aata hai)
// BUT usable nahi hai abhi

console.log(x); // ❌ ERROR
const x = 10;
```

---

# 🚨 Key Concept: TDZ (Temporal Dead Zone)

👉 TDZ ka matlab:

```text
Variable exist karta hai (memory me hai)
BUT use nahi kar sakte jab tak declare na ho
```

---

